# attest — evidence-first engineering

The full skills live under `plugins/attest/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` — the
single source of truth. This rule carries the always-on contract and points
you at the right skill; open that skill's `SKILL.md` and follow its numbered
pass when its trigger matches. Keep this file aligned with `AGENTS.md`.

## Always on — every turn

**Verdict contract.** Never claim work is done, fixed, passing, or correct
without a verdict backed by evidence produced *this turn*:

- **PROVEN** — a command ran this turn and its output confirms the claim; cite it.
- **NOT YET** — evidence says it isn't done; state what's missing.
- **CAN'T PROVE** — unverifiable from here; list it for per-item human acknowledgment.

If nothing is unverified, say "Unverified: none." A test that ran before your
last edit proves nothing about the code now.

**Second-hand results are PLAUSIBLE, never PROVEN** — a subagent's or a
summary's claim is not evidence until you re-ran the decisive command yourself.

**Publish a checklist** for any task of three or more steps, and mark each
step done only when its evidence lands.

**Keep the user fed during long runs** — announce steps likely to exceed a
minute before they start (what's running, when the next update comes — ETAs
from the timings ledger `.claude/attest/timings.local.jsonl` or "unknown",
never invented; append each run's elapsed there), post one-line statuses at
escalating intervals (~1 → ~2 → ~3 min) in quiet stretches, and point
questions at a side chat or second session instead of interrupting —
interrupting discards in-flight work.

## When X → read this skill

| When you are about to… | Follow |
|---|---|
| triage a feature request before it becomes a ticket | `im-a-tpm` |
| find where something lives / how a flow works | `i-explore` |
| establish a fact about a library, API, or platform | `i-research` |
| resolve decisions that are the human's to make | `i-interrogate` |
| shape a module or interface before building | `i-design` |
| plan work before code | `i-plan` |
| run a multi-task plan start to finish | `i-execute` |
| implement a feature or bug fix | `i-code` |
| change structure without changing behavior | `i-refactor` |
| diagnose something broken or slow | `i-debug` |
| change a database schema | `i-migrate` |
| hunt over-engineering / decide what to delete | `i-simplify` |
| review a diff before merge | `im-a-code-reviewer` |
| get a second opinion from a mind that didn't write it | `im-an-adversary` |
| security-review one diff | `im-a-security-reviewer` |
| security-audit a whole codebase | `im-a-security-auditor` |
| review a change for performance / efficiency | `im-a-performance-reviewer` |
| review a UI change | `im-a-design-reviewer` |
| audit developer experience | `im-a-dx-engineer` |
| verify by driving the real app | `im-a-qa-engineer` |
| claim work is complete (exit contract) | `i-attest` |
| turn finished work into a PR | `i-ship` |
| write or update docs | `i-document` |
| set the suite up in a new repo | `i-setup` |

Skills name no stack; per-repo commands and threat model live in
`.claude/attest/project.md` and `security-model.md` (written by `i-setup`).
